---

<V2Layout
  title="Explainer — Quantum Biology DAO"
  description="The Quantum Biology DAO, explained — vision, governance, committees, activities, team, affiliates, and history."
>
  <!-- ====================================================================== -->
  <!-- HERO                                                                   -->
  <!-- ====================================================================== -->
  <section class="relative pt-28 lg:pt-40 pb-16 md:pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-12">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <EyebrowLabel accent="pink">Explainer</EyebrowLabel>
        <h1
          class="font-display text-5xl sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl xl:text-[5rem] leading-[0.95] tracking-tight text-cream-warm"
        >
          The Quantum Biology DAO,
          <em class="italic text-pink/90">explained</em>.
        </h1>
        <p
          class="mt-8 font-sans text-[15px] text-cream leading-relaxed max-w-xl"
        >
          The Quantum Biology DAO is a founder-led community-centric
          organization with the mission of advancing the field of quantum
          biology. It uses a crypto token, QBIO, for governance. The DAO has
          its own budget, committees, and priorities, and is now both the
          largest organization in the field of quantum biology and the premier
          funder, with the best social media profile and the most competitive
          games of quantum biology trivia. Anyone can help us push forward the
          field — just join the <a
            href="https://quantumbiology.community"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class={lk}>Discord</a
          >!
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-start gap-5">
          <V2Cta
            href="https://quantumbiology.community"
            label="Join the community"
            accent="pink"
            external
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ====================================================================== -->
  <!-- BODY                                                                   -->
  <!-- ====================================================================== -->
  <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-12 pb-16 md:pb-24">
    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:gap-7">

      <!-- Table of contents -->
      <article class={bentoCard}>
        <EyebrowLabel accent="pink">Contents</EyebrowLabel>
        <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
          {
            toc.map((t) => (
              <a
                href={t.href}
                class="group flex items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-md border border-cream/10 hover:border-pink/40 hover:bg-pink/5 transition-colors px-4 py-4"
              >
                <span class="font-sans text-[13px] text-cream/85 leading-snug">
                  {t.label}
                </span>
                <svg
                  width="12"
                  height="12"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  class="shrink-0 text-pink/60 group-hover:text-pink transition-colors"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="M5 12h14" />
                  <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
                </svg>
              </a>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- VISION -->
      <article id="vision" class={`${bentoCard} scroll-mt-28`}>
        <EyebrowLabel accent="pink">Vision</EyebrowLabel>
        <h2 class={`${bentoHeading} mb-8`}>
          The <em class="italic text-pink/90">vision</em>.
        </h2>
        <div class={`${bodyText} max-w-3xl`}>
          <p>
            Biology runs on the laws of quantum physics. It’s a hard truth,
            because math is hard, but it’s a necessary one, because we don’t
            get to choose what our biology is or isn’t made of.
          </p>
          <p>
            Quantum mechanics was developed in the early 1900s. It’s been
            almost a hundred years since then. Theorists as early as
            Schrödinger postulated a role for quantum physics in biology.
            Decades have passed, and the evidence for quantum effects in
            biology has mounted. Now, with the help of cutting edge technology
            from quantum sensing and new organizational structures, like the
            Quantum Biology DAO, it is possible to finally investigate quantum
            states inside cells at room temperature and learn how they work.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our goal isn’t just learning, however. We want to change the
            world. The knowledge that comes from advancing the basic science
            of quantum biology will give rise to an entire industry of quantum
            biological applications.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our first stop is biomanufacturing. Companies are growing wheat,
            coffee, and more inside bioreactors specially designed to make
            cells multiply. They aren’t using all of the tools nature gives
            us, though, because they aren’t using quantum. Quantum physics
            explains how weak magnetic fields, like the Earth’s magnetic
            field, which life evolved within, can have effects in biology —
            like cell division rate. Biologists haven’t been able to apply
            magnetic fields to samples, at least, not easily, because they
            haven’t had the instruments or the knowledge of quantum physics.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Quantum Biology DAO is paving the way. We’re building the
            instruments biologists need to work with weak magnetic fields.
            We’re funding the basic science so they can understand the quantum
            states they’re interacting with. You can imagine
            magnetically-powered bioreactors churning out more stuff now and
            in the future when we’re in space or on other planets.
          </p>
          <p>
            Biomanufacturing is just the first step. After that, the real
            target is health. Weak magnetic fields impact many aspects of the
            cells, potentially including cell-wide phenomena such as
            metabolism and apoptosis — which means, keeping cells healthy and
            clearing out senescent cells.
          </p>
          <p>
            Companies are already using weak magnetic fields to improve
            people’s health. Novocure, a publicly traded company with over a
            billion-dollar market cap, uses weak magnetic fields to treat
            cancer. Other companies have used weak magnetic fields to reduce
            symptoms from diabetes. They haven’t been able to systematically
            tune their effects or intelligently search for new ones, though,
            because they don’t have the underlying formulas that tell them how
            quantum effects work in biology.
          </p>
          <p>
            The real future quantum biology offers is one where we, as a
            species, have mastered quantum effects in biology and, along with
            that, weak magnetic field effects. Weak magnetic fields are cheap
            to produce, don’t require surgery or pills, and can be carefully
            targeted and controlled using smart clothing and a cell phone. We
            imagine a future with over-the-air updates making your clothing
            and your environment better able to produce the right sorts of
            magnetic fields to make ourselves healthier, more energetic, and
            able to live a lot longer.
          </p>
          <p>
            Those aren’t the only effects we look forward to. Even though weak
            magnetic fields are important, they aren’t the only point of
            quantum biology. Quantum biology includes prolonging room
            temperature superpositions, something that quantum computing
            desperately needs to learn how to do. It also covers potentially
            more efficient processes for generating energy, like nature
            already does with photosynthesis in the cell, and greater
            knowledge of chemical interactions, including molecular
            recognition which is relevant to drug discovery.
          </p>
          <p>
            Getting to these effects requires serious translational efforts —
            translating basic science to practical applications and
            translating the deep mysteries of quantum physics into a language
            that everyone, including biologists, can understand. The Quantum
            Biology DAO is positioned to perform these translational efforts,
            building new instruments, funding crucial research, and putting
            into place everything else needed for the field of quantum biology
            to succeed and the industry of quantum biology to be born.
          </p>
          <p>Join us! And may the quantum be with you!</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- GOVERNANCE -->
      <article id="governance" class={`${bentoCard} scroll-mt-28`}>
        <EyebrowLabel accent="pink">Governance</EyebrowLabel>
        <h2 class={`${bentoHeading} mb-8`}>
          How the DAO <em class="italic text-pink/90">governs</em>.
        </h2>
        <div class={`${bodyText} max-w-3xl`}>
          <p>
            The Quantum Biology DAO governs by proposals which are made by DAO
            contributors and voted on in accordance with the DAO’s system of
            governance. There are three phases of governance, each intended to
            give different stakeholders a voice. Two of the phases use <a
              href="https://snapshot.box/#/s:qbio.eth/proposal/0x2b40e07d8a0931ecc8a9f3db374484eb16c625a3df3e988de65042b9ae1b5c88"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>QBIO</a
            >, which is an Ethereum-based crypto token, to manage voting
            power. The DAO passes proposals pertaining to governance,
            committees, grants, treasury management, the QBIO token, and any
            other topic related to advancing the field of quantum biology.
          </p>
          <p>
            As a legal entity, the DAO is currently represented by the Quantum
            Biology DAO Association, a Swiss association incorporated in the
            canton of Zug.
          </p>

          <h3 class={h3Class}>Phases of Governance</h3>
          <p>
            The Quantum Biology DAO has three phases of governance, which are
            described in detail in proposals <a
              href="https://snapshot.box/#/s:qbio.eth/proposal/0xedf4358db1235da966d4fa90c1a8faef492dc307a34dfdc9631dfbb1251b0341"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>DP-1</a
            > and <a
              href="https://snapshot.box/#/s:qbio.eth/proposal/0x2b40e07d8a0931ecc8a9f3db374484eb16c625a3df3e988de65042b9ae1b5c88"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>DP-14</a
            >.
          </p>
          <p>
            Phase 1 is <strong class="text-cream-warm">drafting in Discord</strong>.
            In the DAO’s community Discord, there is a <a
              href="https://discord.com/channels/1248368139436163143/1299694115759460362"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>channel</a
            > for proposals. Any member of the community may make a proposal.
            Proposals are typically given their own sub-channel and then
            debated by the community. The authors of the proposals may make
            revisions in response to feedback. Once a sufficient number of 👍s
            are received, including enough from DAO Core Contributors, the
            proposal passes on to Phase 2.
          </p>
          <p>
            Phase 2 is <strong class="text-cream-warm">discussion and voting on Common</strong>.
            The DAO uses a website called <a
              href="https://common.xyz/quantum-biology-dao/discussions?tab=all"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>Common</a
            >, which hosts public discussion and voting by communities. When a
            proposal reaches Phase 2, it is posted to Common. It stays there
            for 1 day (fast), 3 days (normal), or 7 days (slow), depending on
            the speed the proposal was set at. During that time, anyone may
            post a public comment; in order to vote, a person must connect a
            wallet holding 10,000 QBIO. To move from Phase 2 to Phase 3, at
            least 10 votes must be cast and a majority must be in favor. This
            phase is meant to be “1 person, 1 vote” and provides greater power
            to small token holders.
          </p>
          <p>
            Phase 3 is <strong class="text-cream-warm">token voting on Snapshot</strong>.
            For the final phase of governance, the DAO uses a website called <a
              href="https://snapshot.box/#/s:qbio.eth/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>Snapshot</a
            >, which lets people connect their wallets and vote using their
            tokens. To pass Phase 3, at least 3% of tokens must be used vote
            and a majority of votes must be in favor. This phase is meant to
            be “1 token, 1 vote” and provides greater power to large token
            holders.
          </p>
          <p>
            DAO governance can be modified through DAO proposals. This
            happened before, when a flaw in Phase 2 was identified and
            patched.
          </p>

          <h3 class={h3Class}>The QBIO Token</h3>
          <p>
            The Quantum Biology DAO uses a blockchain-based electronic token
            called <a
              href="https://etherscan.io/token/0x3e6a1b21bd267677fa49be6425aebe2fc0f89bde"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>QBIO</a
            > for governance. Tokens were initially auctioned off in December
            2024 in order to raise money for the DAO. Tokens were also given
            to DAO co-founders and to BIO Protocol in return for helping
            incubate and launch the DAO.
          </p>
          <p>
            The QBIO token is now available for purchase on the decentralized
            exchanges <a
              href="https://app.uniswap.org/explore/pools/ethereum/0x4830570554606cBc37478AB773fde991261FD99C"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>Uniswap</a
            > for Ethereum users and <a
              href="https://raydium.io/swap/?inputMint=sol&outputMint=qbioCGDnUBGX5qcK1Fc4zg19GaQEPmxHFMPMZQm4LZ8"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class={lk}>Raydium</a
            > for Solana users. The contract addresses are:
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-pink/70 shrink-0">—</span>
              <span>Ethereum — <code class="font-mono text-[12px] text-cream/70 break-all">0x3e6a1b21bd267677fa49be6425aebe2fc0f89bde</code></span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
